6. CERTIFICATION PATHWAY (DO-178C DAL C / B)
Phase 0: Gap Analysis
· Map ST-T1024 architecture to DO-178C objectives.
· Identify formal verification requirements for the FSM and FIS.
Phase 1: Requirements Capture
· Define system safety goals (e.g., "The system shall not output a false positive on altitude
readings").
· Map goals to FSM states and ROM constants.
Phase 2: Design Assurance
· Implement FSM, ternary engine, and tile isolation.
· Enforce AET ≤ 800 ns with hardware cycle counter.
Phase 3: Verification
· Run formal verification of FSM (model checking).
· Validate hardware timing on FPGA prototype.
· Document all test results.
Phase 4: Certification
· Submit documentation to certification authority (EASA, FAA).
· Engage DER (Designated Engineering Representative) for review.
· Achieve DAL C or B certification.
